  // ===== 英语阅读理解 10篇大题（每篇含5道子题）=====
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read01","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·科普","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"Most of us know about fires, hurricanes, droughts and floods. But from time to time, Mother Nature surprises us, and delivers a weather event that is really weird. Here are some examples of truly strange weather.\n\nOne day in 2005, residents of a small town in Serbia looked out of their windows and saw an unusual sight. It was raining frogs! Without any warning, they found their streets filled with little jumping creatures. Scientists believed a tornado had passed over a lake. It sucked up animals that lived there. The frogs were carried into the air. Then they were dropped in the Serbian town, far away.\n\nAs if tornadoes aren't dangerous enough, some of them can actually be made of fire. When a wildfire reaches very high temperatures, it causes the air to become hot and to rise. Cooler air rushes in to replace the hot air. This creates strong winds. These winds suck up burning plants and even the fire itself. When this happens, a tornado of fire is produced.\n\nIn 1942, hundreds of thousand-year-old skeletons were found under the ice of Lake Roopkund in the Himalayas. Many had holes in their skulls. Scientists think these people were killed by giant hailstones—balls of ice. Hailstones form when raindrops high in the sky turn into pieces of ice. The ice pieces increase in size until the wind cannot hold them up. For the unlucky people at Lake Roopkund, there was nowhere to run. They were all killed by the hailstones.","subQuestions":[{"stem":"A proper title for this passage could be ___.","options":["Humans vs. Nature","Strange Weather","Unusual Tornadoes","Horrible News"],"answer":"Strange Weather"},{"stem":"What is true about the frogs that rained down in Serbia?","options":["The frogs probably fell off a truck.","They fell out of an airplane that exploded.","A tornado took them from a lake and dropped them over the town.","They grew in the clouds and fell down to Earth."],"answer":"A tornado took them from a lake and dropped them over the town."},{"stem":"The words sucked up in Paragraph 2 means ___.","options":["made","lifted","used","blew"],"answer":"lifted"},{"stem":"The word This in Paragraph 3 refers to ___.","options":["the moment when a wildfire grows really big","the moment when rushing winds suck up the fire","the moment when a strong wind is created","the moment when the tornado of fire becomes 15 meters wide"],"answer":"the moment when a strong wind is created"},{"stem":"According to the passage, what's the author's attitude towards weird weather?","options":["It is common and people should not worry about it.","It is exciting to see such strange weather.","It is not very dangerous.","It is terrible and people should be very careful about it."],"answer":"It is terrible and people should be very careful about it."}],"difficulty":2,"difficultyLabel":"中等","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·科普"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·科普"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read02","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·社会","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"Since ancient times, frugality has been one of the traditional virtues among Chinese people. Following this traditional way of life, more young people in China are now looking to frugal, low-cost lifestyles in order to spend less and save more.\n\nThey are beginning to realize and reject the pitfalls of consumerism, believing that simplicity can bring happiness and satisfaction. Economic and employment pressures, as well as changing attitudes toward material life, are also resulting in more young people turning their backs on extravagance and waste.\n\nFrugality is being practiced in a number of ways. Some young people choose discounts and low-priced goods, while others are replacing well-known brands with those that are cost-effective. Some are cautious when buying nonessential items, while others say they save all they can in order to make important purchases.\n\nHe Jiazheng, 22, a college student, said he spends about 10 yuan on each meal and no more than 100 yuan on each item of clothing. He, who is studying economics, said his pursuit of frugality stems from the idea of \"realizing maximum happiness through minimum expenditure.\"","subQuestions":[{"stem":"According to the passage, what lifestyles are more young people expecting to live?","options":["Plain needy lifestyles.","Rich high-cost lifestyles.","Simple low-cost lifestyles.","Extravagant pleasant lifestyles."],"answer":"Simple low-cost lifestyles."},{"stem":"What does the underlined word they (Paragraph 2) refer to?","options":["More young people in China.","More young people in every country.","More young people in any other countries.","More young people in many other countries."],"answer":"More young people in China."},{"stem":"Which is NOT the reason for more young people expecting a frugal life?","options":["Rich and wealthy life.","Economic pressure.","Employment pressures.","Changing attitudes toward material life."],"answer":"Rich and wealthy life."},{"stem":"How many ways of frugality are mentioned in the passage?","options":["2","3","4","5"],"answer":"4"},{"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":["More young people are in pursuit of happiness.","More young people never buy luxury food.","More young people have changed their attitudes toward consumerism.","Frugal, low-cost lifestyles attract a growing number of young people."],"answer":"Frugal, low-cost lifestyles attract a growing number of young people."}],"difficulty":2,"difficultyLabel":"中等","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·社会"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·社会"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read03","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·教育","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"His desire to put what he learned into practice increased after the university established a Luban Workshop in Ethiopia in 2021. The workshop was part of the professional training programs offered by China's vocational education colleges with the aim of sharing expertise.\n\nTo date, Chinese colleges have established 11 Luban Workshops in African countries, offering a wide range of professional training and help for the younger generation in these nations to build up their professional skills.\n\nSome African nations have already benefited from the vocational education cooperation programs. Liu Bin, president of the Alliance for the Development of Luban Workshops, said a crucial factor behind the flourishing vocational training programs is that they seek to meet surging demand for improved local labor forces as Chinese businesses and products go global.\n\nIn Djibouti, the first 24 students trained by a Luban Workshop in fields such as railway operations and rail engineering technology have become interns for the Addis Ababa-Djibouti Railway.\n\nA total of 27 Luban Workshops have been established in 25 countries, most of them in the developing world. The programs provide training in vocational skills tailored to meet the demands of host countries.","subQuestions":[{"stem":"Up to now, how many Luban Workshops have been set up in African countries?","options":["11","24","25","27"],"answer":"11"},{"stem":"What is the purpose of China's Luban Workshop program?","options":["To promote international cooperation on higher education.","To promote international cooperation on vocational education.","To promote cross-institution cooperation on higher education.","To promote cross-institution cooperation on vocational education."],"answer":"To promote international cooperation on vocational education."},{"stem":"According to the passage, which help is NOT offered by the Chinese colleges?","options":["Sharing equipment.","Providing financial supports.","Providing training for teachers.","Sharing teaching methods and materials."],"answer":"Providing financial supports."},{"stem":"Why did China start the first Luban Workshop in Africa?","options":["To help maintain and operate the railway.","To help train talent, which is in short supply.","To help train students, which are in short supply.","To help train senior engineers, which are in short supply."],"answer":"To help train talent, which is in short supply."},{"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":["Luban Workshops are specially made programs provided by China.","Luban Workshops have trained 24 students in Djibouti.","Luban Workshops have been beneficial to African vocational education.","Luban Workshops have offered degrees to students in Africa."],"answer":"Luban Workshops have been beneficial to African vocational education."}],"difficulty":2,"difficultyLabel":"中等","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·教育"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·教育"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read04","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·教育","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"College professors these days face an ever-higher bar to grab the attention of their students, forced to compete with the pulling power of smartphones and laptops in large lecture halls. But when your professor is a social media star, it is a little bit easier.\n\nTatiana Erukhimova, who teaches physics at Texas A&M University, has managed to get her students, as well as future generations, excited about the science. Known as \"Dr. Tatiana\" to her students and online fan base, the professor performs physics tricks with boundless energy and enthusiasm. Videos of her theatrical demonstrations have attracted hundreds of millions of views across social media platforms.\n\nWhen she first started teaching college freshman classes almost two decades ago, she says she struggled to grab the attention of her younger students. By junior year, students majoring in physics are committed to learning. But when it comes to teaching a large lecture hall of 100-plus first-year students, first impressions are make or break.\n\n\"I did not grab their attention on the first day—that was my mistake,\" she says. \"I missed this opportunity to bond with them from the very beginning.\" By the second semester, she adjusted her approach to make her lecture halls feel smaller, and get her students engaged.\n\nThe key, she says, has been to make herself approachable and her instruction personal. \"Talk to your students before and after class, walk up and down the stairs when you teach your class rather than stay on the stage. And don't just lecture, talk to them—make it interactive.\"","subQuestions":[{"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, professors find it more difficult to ___.","options":["use smartphones in class","become social media stars","get students' attention in class","give lectures without using laptops"],"answer":"get students' attention in class"},{"stem":"What can we learn about Dr. Tatiana from Paragraph 2?","options":["She is a professor of online games.","She performs physics experiments in theatres.","She gains less energy from social media platforms.","She has made many young people interested in physics."],"answer":"She has made many young people interested in physics."},{"stem":"Which is closest in meaning to \"make or break\" in Paragraph 4?","options":["Normal.","Crucial.","Breakable.","Successful."],"answer":"Crucial."},{"stem":"According to Paragraph 5, Dr. Tatiana ___.","options":["found the lecture hall too small","made a mistake in the second semester","got her students engaged at the very beginning","could reflect on and adjust her teaching accordingly"],"answer":"could reflect on and adjust her teaching accordingly"},{"stem":"According to the last paragraph, good teachers should ___.","options":["give lectures in an interactive way","persuade students to stay on the stage","ask questions that most students cannot answer","force students to get well prepared before class"],"answer":"give lectures in an interactive way"}],"difficulty":2,"difficultyLabel":"中等","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·教育"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·教育"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read05","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·社会","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"This is one of two schools in Richmond where the city has installed new enforcement cameras to catch speeders. Fitz Patrick has two children at the school. She is also a traffic safety advocate for the nonprofit Greater Richmond Fit4Kids, which is why she owns a radar gun.\n\nStill, Fitz Patrick has mixed feelings about the speed cameras. She would rather see the whole street redesigned to discourage speeding and protect walkers and bicyclists. But she also knows that will not happen anytime soon.\n\nThe number of traffic deaths has risen sharply over the past decade, and safety advocates around the country are desperately searching for anything that will get drivers to slow down. But critics say speed cameras can be a financial burden on those who are least able to pay. Still, they have earned the support of important safety advocates, including Jonathan Adkins, the chief executive officer of the Governors Highway Safety Association.\n\nPolice departments in many places have scaled down their traffic enforcement, Adkins says, and speeding and careless driving seem to be getting worse. He says automated cameras can help fill that blank. \"The question is, how do we arrange them in a fair way with the public support?\"","subQuestions":[{"stem":"Fitz Patrick has a radar gun because ___.","options":["she is a traffic safety advocate","she has two children at the school","she has new cameras to catch speeders","she is a school headmaster in Richmond"],"answer":"she is a traffic safety advocate"},{"stem":"According to Paragraph 2, Fitz Patrick thinks that ___.","options":["more speed cameras will soon be fixed","redesigning the whole street is a better choice","state lawmakers should redesign speed cameras","the newly-installed cameras encourage speeding"],"answer":"redesigning the whole street is a better choice"},{"stem":"What is the main idea of Paragraph 3?","options":["Drivers find speed cameras can protect their safety.","There are different views on the use of speed cameras.","Safety advocates are desperately searching for slow drivers.","Critics believe speed cameras are a good solution."],"answer":"There are different views on the use of speed cameras."},{"stem":"What is Jonathan Adkins' attitude toward installing speed cameras?","options":["Critical.","Supportive.","Doubtful.","Unconcerned."],"answer":"Supportive."},{"stem":"According to the passage, speed cameras are used to ___.","options":["sponsor the state law","improve the traffic flow in the city","reduce traffic deaths and slow drivers down","make money for the government"],"answer":"reduce traffic deaths and slow drivers down"}],"difficulty":3,"difficultyLabel":"较难","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·社会"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·社会"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read06","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·健康","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"Experts suggest that Americans stop worrying about getting a perfect eight hours of sleep, and warn that stressing about the magic number may actually result in a drop in sleep quality and duration.\n\nDr. Reena Mehra, a director of sleep research at the Cleveland Clinic, held that focusing too much on falling asleep may interrupt the process. \"It works against the individual,\" she said.\n\nAccording to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, more than a third of Americans do not achieve the recommended seven to nine hours of sleep per night. The agency also found that quality sleep is determined by major sleep episodes that do not have frequent awakenings.\n\nOne paper looking into the ideal amount of sleep found that \"Sleep duration recommendations issued by public health authorities help to inform the population of interventions, policies, and healthy sleep behaviors. However, the ideal amount of sleep required each night can vary between different individuals due to gene-related factors and other reasons, and it is important to adapt our recommendations on a case-by-case basis.\"\n\nIn the past, a lack of sleep was a sign to bosses that a person was productive and successful. But today, people try to create strategies to make the best use of their rest. Researchers, scientists, psychologists and individuals in the sleep business said that the best course of action when it comes to sleep is to relax.","subQuestions":[{"stem":"In writing Paragraph 2, the author aims to ___.","options":["give a definition","draw a conclusion","make a comparison","support a viewpoint"],"answer":"support a viewpoint"},{"stem":"According to Paragraph 4, the ideal amount of sleep required each night ___.","options":["can affect genes","is based on policies","is different from person to person","should be revised by public authorities"],"answer":"is different from person to person"},{"stem":"According to Paragraph 5, in the past, a person lacking sleep was probably regarded as ___.","options":["an old person","a productive and successful person","a person creating strategies","a person making good use of his rest"],"answer":"a productive and successful person"},{"stem":"What is the best title for this passage?","options":["How to Get Eight Hours of Sleep","Stop Stressing About the Perfect Sleep Number","The Importance of Sleep","Sleep Problems in America"],"answer":"Stop Stressing About the Perfect Sleep Number"},{"stem":"Where is the passage most probably taken from?","options":["An essay on trade.","A report of public health.","A review of a sports event.","An introduction to an agency."],"answer":"A report of public health."}],"difficulty":2,"difficultyLabel":"中等","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·健康"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·健康"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read07","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·励志","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"From now on, never spend your precious time thinking of reasons for your failures and shortcomings. Instead, realize that the seeds of success were planted within you when you were born. Only you have the power to make those seeds grow.\n\nThe seeds, and the power to grow them, are contained in the most awesome machine ever created: the human mind. Success is a choice and not a chance. You were born a winner. You were born rich. You can be a success as long as you make the right choice.\n\nYou cannot be successful without first developing your self-esteem. Your level of self-esteem is always based on the degree of control that you are able to exercise over yourself, and thus over your life. People with low self-esteem are people who do not believe that they have any power, or responsibility for their lives. They are the perennial victims and martyrs. They are leaves tossed by the winds of chance and blown about with any sudden change in the weather.\n\nYou can exercise control over your life only to the degree that you believe that you are responsible for everything that happens in your life. Failures think that everything happens by accident and by chance. Successful people realize that they are responsible.\n\nEverything happens as a result of something. If we can identify the cause, we can control the effect. We are responsible for what we choose to think and believe. One generally rises to the level that one expects. We are responsible for setting our expectations. Our success is dependent upon our level of confidence.","subQuestions":[{"stem":"People with low self-esteem are compared to leaves because they ___.","options":["are ready to change their minds","are easily affected by windy weather","don't have the power to face their fate","can't exercise control over themselves"],"answer":"can't exercise control over themselves"},{"stem":"Losers would think that ___.","options":["success is the result of hard work","working hard will lead to success","their failure is only because of bad luck","they don't make efforts to succeed"],"answer":"their failure is only because of bad luck"},{"stem":"It can be learned from Paragraph 5 that ___.","options":["whether we will succeed depends on our level of confidence","developing confidence depends on future success","thoughts and beliefs are the result of creative mind","setting our expectations is essential before taking action"],"answer":"whether we will succeed depends on our level of confidence"},{"stem":"The last paragraph serves as ___.","options":["the proof of the author's point","the conclusion of the argument","an introduction to another topic","a comparison between two views"],"answer":"the conclusion of the argument"},{"stem":"Which is the best title for the passage?","options":["Success Is a Choice","The Secrets of Success","Develop Our Confidence","How to Achieve Success"],"answer":"Success Is a Choice"}],"difficulty":1,"difficultyLabel":"基础","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·励志"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·励志"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read08","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·科技","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"The QR code system originated in Japan. The engineer Masahiro Hara felt the limitations of the one-dimensional bar codes in use and thus developed QR codes, which could carry data both horizontally and vertically. QR codes could hold much more information than bar codes due to their extra dimension.\n\nIn addition, QR codes have larger data capacity, smaller printout size and higher resistance to damage. Though the technology behind QR codes is complicated, we can easily create our own QR codes with the help of QR code generators, many of which are available online for free.\n\nUsers could enter the data they wish the QR code to display, and the generator turns it into a symbol that can be printed or displayed electronically. The process of creating QR codes could be really fun when we customize the design according to our specific needs. For instance, we can adjust the color and add a logo.\n\nMoreover, dynamic QR codes are also available. They are more versatile than standard QR codes because they allow users to edit data entered previously, whereas data in standard QR codes cannot be edited once printed. Besides, don't limit your QR code to one mobile scanner. Anyone can scan your code with any reader. A lower barrier to entry makes success more likely for you and the user.","subQuestions":[{"stem":"Where did the QR code system originate?","options":["China.","Japan.","America.","Germany."],"answer":"Japan."},{"stem":"What is the advantage of QR codes over bar codes?","options":["They are smaller in size.","They can hold more information.","They are cheaper to print.","They are easier to scan."],"answer":"They can hold more information."},{"stem":"How can we create our own QR codes?","options":["By buying expensive software.","By using QR code generators online.","By learning complicated technology.","By hiring a professional engineer."],"answer":"By using QR code generators online."},{"stem":"What is the difference between dynamic QR codes and standard QR codes?","options":["Dynamic QR codes are smaller.","Dynamic QR codes can be edited after printing.","Standard QR codes have more data capacity.","Standard QR codes are more versatile."],"answer":"Dynamic QR codes can be edited after printing."},{"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":["The history of bar codes.","The features and uses of QR codes.","How to scan QR codes.","The disadvantages of QR codes."],"answer":"The features and uses of QR codes."}],"difficulty":2,"difficultyLabel":"中等","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·科技"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·科技"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read09","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·科普","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"We all know that drugstores where you can buy medicine when you're sick are very useful inventions. But how did people get medicine in ancient times? They got medicine from nature, mostly from plants. In fact, the study of plants started out as a section of medicine. To this day, many people around the world still get their medicine from plants.\n\nPlants are full of chemicals—ones that they produce themselves. These are not intended for medicinal use. Plants can't move around as we do, so they use chemicals to accomplish a lot of their most basic life functions—everything from fighting off fierce animals to communicating, and to producing the young.\n\nLong ago, humans learned that these same chemicals affect our bodies. Some make us sick or even kill us, but many are beneficial. Early people must have discovered them through trial and error, and also by watching animals. Scientists know that some animals treat themselves with plants when they are sick. Bears in North America have been observed to dig up the roots of a plant, chew the roots, and then spread them all over their fur.\n\nOver time, humans developed great skills at diagnosing conditions and knowing just which plants to prescribe and how to prepare them. Much knowledge about those plants wasn't written down, so with the arrival of modern medicine, some of what people used to know was lost.","subQuestions":[{"stem":"How did people get medicine in ancient times?","options":["From drugstores.","From animals.","From modern medicine.","From nature, mostly from plants."],"answer":"From nature, mostly from plants."},{"stem":"Why do plants produce chemicals?","options":["To provide food for people.","To meet their basic needs.","To provide animals with medicine.","To make themselves look beautiful."],"answer":"To meet their basic needs."},{"stem":"Early people acquired the knowledge of medicinal plants by ___.","options":["digging up plants","keeping animals as pets","trial and error and watching animals","reading medical books"],"answer":"trial and error and watching animals"},{"stem":"Why has some knowledge about medicinal plants been lost?","options":["Because plants disappeared.","Because it was not written down.","Because modern medicine is better.","Because people don't need plants anymore."],"answer":"Because it was not written down."},{"stem":"What is the main idea of the passage?","options":["Drugstores are useful inventions.","Plants produce chemicals for their own use.","Medicine originally came from plants in nature.","Bears know how to use plants as medicine."],"answer":"Medicine originally came from plants in nature."}],"difficulty":2,"difficultyLabel":"中等","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·科普"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·科普"});
  window.STUDY_DATA.questions.push({"id":"read-read10","module":"public","subject":"英语","chapter":"ch-en-reading","knowledgePoint":"阅读理解·职场","type":"reading","typeLabel":"阅读","stem":"请阅读下面的短文，然后回答5道选择题。","passage":"Working from home comes with some additional benefits. You enjoy a better work-life balance and don't have to commute to the office. You can work in casual clothes if you want. Designing your home office space can produce a positive effect, too—if you don't want to be stuck in a crowded room all day.\n\nHere are two ideas to help you design the ultimate home office.\n\nChoose your color. While some people like bright colors, you might not want to see yellow or green every day. Paint your office walls in a neutral color to give your eyes a break. You should also avoid darker colors, which tend to make small spaces look even smaller. This doesn't mean your home office needs to be completely neutral. Add something like a framed artwork.\n\nPlay with natural light. You might push your desk into a dark corner, creating an office cubicle. Working in a small space can make your home office feel much more oppressive than it needs to be. Instead, look for areas where natural light flows in your home. Move your desk close to windows while keeping it parallel to them to reduce glare. You can also add curtains to help you manage the amount of light that enters your workspace each day, particularly around lunchtime.","subQuestions":[{"stem":"According to the first paragraph, if you work from home, you can ___.","options":["earn more money","have a better work-life balance","work fewer hours","get promoted faster"],"answer":"have a better work-life balance"},{"stem":"The writer believes that designing one's home office space can ___.","options":["produce a positive effect","waste a lot of money","make work more stressful","take up too much time"],"answer":"produce a positive effect"},{"stem":"Why are you advised not to use darker colors when designing your office space?","options":["Because dark colors are expensive.","Because dark colors make small spaces look even smaller.","Because dark colors are bad for eyes.","Because dark colors fade quickly."],"answer":"Because dark colors make small spaces look even smaller."},{"stem":"The word oppressive in Paragraph 4 means ___.","options":["relaxed","interested","uncomfortable","flexible"],"answer":"uncomfortable"},{"stem":"The purpose of adding curtains in your home office is to ___.","options":["make the room look nicer","manage the amount of light","keep the room warm","reduce noise from outside"],"answer":"manage the amount of light"}],"difficulty":2,"difficultyLabel":"中等","source":"reading-comprehension","tags":["阅读理解","阅读理解·职场"],"analysis":"【参考答案】请逐题作答后查看答案解析","hint":"阅读理解·阅读理解·职场"});

